From ffe1787ea58214d1a7c4d8c9d6369c899f60ca69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:22:04 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 21/24] VideoOutput: draw the views of a video with its depth
 map

A frame in a depth layout holds a picture with its depth map (2D plus
depth): the FFmpeg backend says so in the frame's StereoMode, and packs a
depth layer or depth stream with its picture. VideoOutput showed such a
frame as it is stored, picture and depth map side by side.

Draw the two views from it with libstereo-dibr (depth-image-based
rendering, Sparky Stereo OS's stereo-layer 1.9.0) into a frame of the same
pixel format, both views at the picture's size, the left eye first, and
show that as full side by side 3D video: each eye its view on a 3D
compositor, the eye chosen elsewhere (stereoView), the eyes swapped by
stereoSwapEyes. Every layout of the depth marks is read
(depthSideBySidePictureFirst and DepthFirst, depthTopBottomPictureFirst
and DepthFirst, depthGraphicsTopBottom with graphics over the picture,
depthBackgroundQuarters with the background filling what the picture
uncovers), in planar, semi-planar and 32 bit RGB formats of 8 to 16 bits.

What a depth sample means is, first to last: the user's Stereo3DDepth mark
(stereoDepthMark), the user's meaning (stereoDepthMeaning with
stereoDepthNear and stereoDepthFar), the stream's mark, then nearness. A
malformed mark shows the picture alone (docs/depth-marks.md, rule 1), as
does stereoDepth set to false; StereoFlat shows the frame as stored.
Every choice of libstereo-dibr is a property: the picture as the left eye
or the middle (stereoDepthView), forward, backward or layered warping
(stereoDepthWarp), the fill of what the views uncover (stereoDepthFill,
with stereoDepthRadius), the smoothing of the depth (stereoDepthSmooth,
stereoDepthSigmaH, stereoDepthSigmaV), the range, the screen position and
a shift (stereoDepthRange, stereoDepthZero, stereoDepthShift). A choice
that changes redraws a paused frame. The depth layouts are stereoInput
values too, for a video that does not say it.

Without libstereo-dibr (pkg-config stereo-dibr >= 1.9.0) the picture is
shown alone.

The test draws frames of every layout with a disc nearer than a box nearer
than the background, and measures the shift of each between the views
against the parallax the convention gives; marks of the user and of the
file, and malformed ones, are checked the same way.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code
(cherry picked from commit a78b9b91f3b15a4c81a47bc1bbba4fa8b7bf78f0)
